<title>INDIA: India's M3 money supply eases to 15.9 pct on Jan 3.</title>
<headline>India's M3 money supply eases to 15.9 pct on Jan 3.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-01-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>India's year-on-year M3 money supply growth was 15.9 percent on January 3,1997, down from 16.2 percent in the previous fortnight, the Reserve Bank of India (RBI) said in its weekly statistical supplement on Monday.  </p>
<p>		   M3 MONEY SUPPLY GROWTH (yr-on-yr in pct)</p>
<p>		   Jan 3, 1997    Dec 20,1996  Jan 5, 1996</p>
<p>		   15.9	     16.2	    15.12</p>
<p>Money supply was 6,637.85 billion rupees on January 3, 1997 compared to 6,589.30 billion rupees on December 20, 1996, the RBI said.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
</text>
